how to bounce back after failure  so i got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers love you guys  who was ed d who wrote in to say hey  evan hypothetically speaking  say you started a new business it was a  complete failure gained  a tone of something that was some ways  to get you back on your feet and start  another business both emotionally and  physically so  anyways wonder how do i get back on my  feet after i fail what's the best way to  do an emotion physically  this is a great question because a lot  of entrepreneurs deal with failure and  you will know  failure everybody will know failure  before you achieve success  for me there are two types of failure  the first is going to be where you've  started a business and you shut it down  completely shut it down moved on and did  something else  the second is you're in your business  and  what's what you're trying to do right  now isn't working and you need to change  your model you change what you're  selling  change how you're selling it says all  these failures that you reach before you  have success  and if you look at the stories of famous  entrepreneurs you'll find that they all  went through the same things like  every entrepreneur had failures before  they became successful  so here's what will help you okay and it  centers around  belief no surprise coming from me the  first part is  believe that you're doing the right  thing a lot of times the failed  companies you started for  not the right motives you started just  trying to make a lot of money you  started because you  still thought it'd be a great  opportunity but you didn't start it  because  you had a burning passion for this and  that's where most businesses will fail  you have to really believe that you're  doing the right thing like this is  something that is needed  and you are going to will this thing  into into creation it needs to be done  you love it that much  the second is believe that you can do it  you know i think that's going to be one  of the hardest parts if all you've had  is failure in your life believe that you  can do it  and the easiest way that i found to  start getting that belief back in  yourself is small wins  because when you see this huge gap in  where you want to go where you want to  be and where you are now you see this  massive gap  and that can be so so scary  and you have no track record to say that  you can bridge that gap  that you you're just you know  you're listening to the little man you  are just mired in self-defeat and you  think there's no way i can get there  the way to do that is to make the steps  smaller and you go one step  and then that's easy enough to do again  and another step but another step but  another step  until you've gone all the way and you  don't realize what a big step you've  taken  anything that you're gonna do that's  that's worthwhile doing is going to come  with a healthy dose of fear  and i remember just as an example you  know my goal is to help a billion  entrepreneurs and  i was invited to speak in brunei one  year  in asia and i didn't realize how big an  event was going to be it was going to be  uh you know huge room like a thousand  people it's going to be broadcast on  their national television  and i was nervous you know and i  secretly wish that they would call me  and say  but it's off you don't have to come  forget that you know the day before  some big thing you secretly wish it  would be canceled  and i realized you know what this is  this is important for our mission  and i got out there i did a great job i  loved it it was such a high such a rush  and  i left feeling like i could do that  again like that was scary for me the  first time  but i could do it again i could do it  again i could do it again so push  yourself to take these little steps  and you'll gain confidence and greater  belief in yourself to be able to go up  and do  you know eventually achieve that gap  and the last one is believe that that it  can be done and  a lot of times all you'll see is  darkness around you a lot of times  you may not you know have the full  confidence that this thing is going to  work out  and what really helped me with that is  reading the stories of famous  entrepreneurs i love famous  entrepreneurs stories i love the bios i  love seeing how they got started  and all of them had this belief that it  was going to work out and reading their  stories and seeing how they failed and  seeing how nobody believed in them and  seeing how they had all these crisis  you look at them now i think of any  entrepreneur you look at jobs or disney  or  gates or whoever it is when they started  it looked like they had no hope  and they turned something amazing out of  it  and so reading those stories of the  early days made me  believe that even though it doesn't make  sense quite yet now  that the dots will line up in my future  then it will work out and you have to  have that same belief  so hopefully that helps my three steps  to helping you get back on your feet  and maybe one final one is know that  you're not alone you know it's dirty  secret of entrepreneurship is that  nobody likes to talk about their  failures you only talk about the wins  right you're meeting somebody in the  face saying  here's all the great stuff that happened  but nobody says ah man  i'm thinking of shutting down this  company i don't know what to do  everybody's had failures everybody's  been through this you are not alone  and you can come through if you believe  thank you guys for watching you liked  the video give it a thumbs up below  you want to leave a comment you have a  question for me leave it below  wish me to feel better leave it below uh  click on my face to subscribe to the  channel  and thank you so much i'll see
 

